---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../../components/SiteFooter.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Industrial software at HEIG-VD · Nelson Jeanrenaud"
  description="My work at HEIG-VD: software architecture, .NET operator interfaces, PLC integration over ADS, and a WPF digital twin for automated hydroponic lettuce production."
>
  <SiteHeader />
  <main class="wrap heig" id="top">
    <header class="heig__intro">
      <a class="heig__back" href="/#work">Back to work experience</a>
      <p class="kicker">HEIG-VD · Institute of Industrial Automation</p>
      <h1>Industrial control software<br />and a digital twin</h1>
      <p class="heig__lead">
        Turning the requirements of an automated hydroponic lettuce installation into
        operator interfaces, machine integration, and software that can be tested in simulation.
      </p>
      <dl class="heig__facts">
        <div><dt>Role</dt><dd>R&amp;D Collaborator</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Period</dt><dd>April 2025 – Present</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Location</dt><dd>Yverdon-les-Bains, Switzerland</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </header>

    <section class="heig__section" aria-labelledby="context-title">
      <p class="kicker">Context</p>
      <h2 id="context-title">Software for a physical installation</h2>
      <p>
        At HEIG-VD's Institute of Industrial Automation, I work on control software for
        an AI-optimized hydroponic lettuce installation with industrial partner
        <a href="https://www.techponics.ag/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Techponics</a>.
        The software connects PLCs, cameras, and AI models and orchestrates the installation's
        operation through a web interface.
      </p>
      <p>
        The work brings together application development, automation, and AI. My focus is the
        software architecture and full-stack implementation. I coordinate integration and
        technical decisions with automation engineers, AI engineers, and electronics engineers.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="heig__section" aria-labelledby="contribution-title">
      <p class="kicker">My contribution</p>
      <h2 id="contribution-title">From requirements to implementation</h2>
      <ul class="heig__contributions">
        <li><strong>Requirements and modelling.</strong> Work with the team to define use cases and how the installation's
          processes should operate. Translate these decisions into requirements and specifications,
          domain models, and UML designs.</li>
        <li><strong>Application architecture.</strong> Structure the C#/.NET software using object-oriented
          design and clean architecture principles.</li>
        <li><strong>Web HMI.</strong> Build a modern web interface with Blazor so operators can interact
          with the installation.</li>
        <li><strong>PLC integration.</strong> Interface with the PLCs over ADS, working with automation
          engineers to connect application behaviour and machine control.</li>
        <li><strong>Plugin framework.</strong> Design an extension framework so installation configuration
          can be extended with separate DLL modules without recompiling the core application.</li>
        <li><strong>Digital twin.</strong> Develop a real-time 3D simulation in WPF with time acceleration
          and fault simulation for testing machine behaviour.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="heig__section" aria-labelledby="system-title">
      <p class="kicker">System overview</p>
      <h2 id="system-title">Application, machine control, simulation</h2>
      <dl class="heig__systems">
        <div>
          <dt>Web HMI and orchestration <span>ASP.NET Core · Blazor</span></dt>
          <dd>The web interface supports operators, while the application connects PLCs, cameras,
            and AI models to orchestrate the installation.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Machine integration <span>ADS · PLC</span></dt>
          <dd>ADS connects the software to the PLC. I work with automation engineers on the
            interface between application behaviour and machine control.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Extensible installation configuration <span>DLL plugins</span></dt>
          <dd>The plugin framework keeps configuration extensions in separate software modules.
            New modules can be added to extend an installation's configuration without rebuilding
            the core application.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Digital twin <span>WPF · C#</span></dt>
          <dd>A real-time 3D simulation represents machine behaviour, with time acceleration
            and fault simulation to support testing.</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </section>

    <section class="heig__section" aria-labelledby="testing-title">
      <p class="kicker">Engineering focus</p>
      <h2 id="testing-title">Testing beyond the real hardware</h2>
      <p>
        Software for a physical installation needs a way to examine machine behaviour while
        development and integration are still underway. The digital twin gives this work a
        virtual test environment alongside the PLC integration. Time acceleration helps examine
        behaviour over longer simulated periods, while fault simulation allows abnormal conditions
        to be explored.
      </p>
      <p>
        Simulation supports preparation and investigation; it does not replace validation on
        the installation. The software still needs to be checked against the behaviour of
        the actual equipment during integration.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="heig__section" aria-labelledby="status-title">
      <p class="kicker">Ongoing work</p>
      <h2 id="status-title">Development and integration</h2>
      <p>
        This is an ongoing R&amp;D role. Alongside implementation, I contribute to planning,
        testing, and integration with the project stakeholders.
      </p>
      <p><a href="/cv/nelson-jeanrenaud-cv.pdf">Download my CV</a> for an overview of my experience.</p>
    </section>

    <p class="heig__closing"><a href="/#work">Back to work experience</a></p>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .heig__intro { padding: clamp(2.5rem, 7vw, 4rem) 0 2.5rem; }
  .heig__back { display: inline-block; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.8rem; margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }
  .heig h1 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 1.5rem + 2vw, 2.8rem); line-height: 1.15; letter-spacing: -0.025em; margin: 0 0 1.25rem; }
  .heig__lead { color: var(--text-dim); }
  .heig__facts { border-top: 1px solid var(--border); margin: 1.8rem 0 0; padding-top: 1.2rem; }
  .heig__facts > div { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 5rem 1fr; gap: 0.7rem; margin: 0.3rem 0; }
  .heig__facts dt { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--text-dim); padding-top: 0.2rem; }
  .heig__facts dd { margin: 0; }
  .heig__section { padding: 2.5rem 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .heig__section p, .heig__contributions { color: var(--text-dim); }
  .heig__contributions { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.2rem; }
  .heig__contributions li { padding-left: 0.2rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .heig__contributions li:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .heig__systems { margin: 0; }
  .heig__systems > div { padding: 1.2rem 1.4rem; border: 1px solid var(--border-strong); border-left: 2px solid var(--green); background: var(--bg-soft); margin: 0 0 0.8rem; }
  .heig__systems dt { font-weight: 500; line-height: 1.5; }
  .heig__systems dt span { display: block; font-family: var(--mono); color: var(--text-dim); font-size: 0.78rem; margin-top: 0.25rem; font-weight: 400; }
  .heig__systems dd { margin: 0.7rem 0 0; color: var(--text-dim); }
  .heig__closing { padding: 0.5rem 0 3rem; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.85rem; }
  @media (max-width: 30rem) {
    .heig__facts > div { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0; margin-bottom: 0.8rem; }
    .heig__systems > div { padding: 1rem; }
  }
</style>
